s  i know this was a response to when  victims wind up in the hospital but you  also talk a very about a very important  training prior to that part the public  training of stopping the bleed  absolutely  because  mass shootings any other sort of mass  casualty can happen without notice in  any location  so it's really important for the public  to understand what they can do  and in our own shooting there were many  many valiant acts to try to save lives  stop the bleed training actually was  introduced by the american college of  surgeons  after the sandy hook  shooting  and it teaches basic principles of  hemorrhage control how to apply a  tourniquet adequately if you don't have  one what else you can use and how to  apply pressure to a bleeding wound  these maneuvers can save lives yeah and  we've had plenty of those trainings  across our valley and you can always go  online to find the next one nearest you  if you would like to become trained in  that way as well dr kuhls thank you so  much for your time we greatly appreciate  you're very welcome
 

